  interestingFactsEn: "Herman Minkovsky's life is full of remarkable coincidences, irony, and vivid episodes that show him as a brilliant, witty and a little arrogant scientist.\n\n♪ Wunderkind, who defeated academicians at 17 years of age, while still a student, Minkovsky solved the difficult task of the Paris Academy of Sciences of presenting the number as the sum of five squares, and his work was so deep that it went far beyond the question and contained a common theory of square forms.Academic Charles Ermit, one of the greatest mathematicians of the time, was so impressed that he wrote to a young genius: \"I am filled with surprise and admiration in front of your principles and results... you are opening up to me a sort of a whole new arithmetic world.\" A 17-year-old Russian empire boy received the Grand Prix of the Academy and instruction from academic Marie Enmon Jordan: \"Work, please, to become an outstanding mathematician.\"\n\nEinstein is probably the most famous chicken in his life story. From 1896 to 1902, Minkovsky taught at the Zurich Polytechnic, and Albert Einstein was among his students. Minkovsky said, \"This Einstein, he's always skipped my lectures... I would never believe what he was capable of.\" He called a former student \"lazy dog\" and said that \"he never bothered to be math.Ironically, it is this \"unhappy\" student who, after just a few years, will glorify Minkowski by creating a mathematical basis for his theory, and there is even an interesting (and perhaps apocryphal) story about how Minkowski gave Einstein an incredible equation to \"learning\" him, but Einstein did brilliantly.\n\nThe joke over the storm and the \"four paint problem\" of Minkovsky was known for his sharp mind and sense of humor. He once told the students that he hoped to prove the famous problem of four colors (if four colors are enough to paint any map).After several weeks of unsuccessful attempts to enter the audience under the thunderstorms, he said quite seriously: \"The heavens are angry with my impudence: my proof of the problem of four flowers is also wrong.\" Only then did he smile and begin the lecture.\n\nThe contribution of a medical brother in Herman's shadow often remains his older brother Oscar Minkovsky, a famous doctor. It was Oscar who experimented in 1889 with the removal of the pancreas in a dog, which led to the development of diabetes mellitus in the animal, which proved the link between pancreas iron and diabetes and laid the foundation for future insulin discovery.\n\nIn one film, the creators showed Einstein's encounter with Minkovsky at the Zalzburg Convention in September 1909, where the professor remembers his \"lazy student.\" The problem is that the real Herman Minkowski died of an appendix in January 1909.Thus, in the film \"Professor Minkovsky\" spoke to his ghost, the creators sacrificed historical accuracy to the artistic design.\n\nHis main phrase, which became a prophecy on 21 September 1908 in Cologne, Minkovsky, gave his famous speech \"Spatial and Time\", which permanently changed physics. His key phrase sounds like a poetic manifesto of a new era: > \"The space itself and time itself must turn to fiction, and only some kind of connection between both must still be self-sufficient.\"This speech was immediately described as a grand \"piar action\" of new physics, after which even distant people spoke about relativity."
